<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 20 May, from 325 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">325 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,701 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Council of Nicaea opens under Constantine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> from across the empire gathered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> in the first ecumenical council of the Church. It condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a> and produced the first version of the Nicene Creed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1498">1498 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">528 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vasco da Gama reaches Calicut in India</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Da Gama's fleet arrived on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s Malabar coast after sailing around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. The sea route he opened allowed Portugal to bypass the overland spice trade and build an Asian empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calicut">Calicut</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1570">1570 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">456 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ortelius publishes the first modern atlas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abraham Ortelius issued the Theatrum Orbis Terrarum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>, a bound collection of uniform maps covering the known world. It became a bestseller and went through many editions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1802">1802 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">224 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon restores slavery in French colonies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A law of the Consulate maintained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> where it had not been abolished and paved the way for its return elsewhere, reversing the Revolution's abolition of 1794. Resistance helped drive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> to independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1873">1873 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">153 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Levi Strauss and Jacob Davis patent riveted denim trousers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The patent for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> rivets at the stress points of work trousers marked the birth of blue jeans. Made for labourers in the American West, they became a global garment.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1927">1927 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">99 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Lindbergh takes off for Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lindbergh left Roosevelt Field, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, in the Spirit of St Louis. He landed at Le Bourget 33.5 hours later, completing the first solo non-stop transatlantic flight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Amelia Earhart sets off on her solo Atlantic flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Earhart took off from Harbour Grace, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>, and landed in a field near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Derry</a> the next day. She became the first woman to fly solo across the Atlantic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First prisoners are brought to Auschwitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thirty German criminal prisoners arrived from Sachsenhausen to act as camp functionaries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a> grew into the largest Nazi death camp, where about 1.1 million people, most of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, were murdered.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-thornton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-thornton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Thornton</span><span class="tp">1759–1828</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-stuart-mill"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-stuart-mill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Stuart Mill</span><span class="tp">1806–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-mujica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-mujica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Mujica</span><span class="tp">1935–2025</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/goh-chok-tong"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Goh Chok Tong</span><span class="tp">b. 1941</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vladimiro-montesinos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vladimiro-montesinos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vladimiro Montesinos</span><span class="tp">b. 1945</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ecgfrith-of-northumbria"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Ecgfrith of Northumbria</span><span class="tp">c. 645–685</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aethelberht-ii-of-east-anglia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aethelberht-ii-of-east-anglia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Æthelberht II of East Anglia</span><span class="tp">d. 794</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gero-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gero-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gero the Great</span><span class="tp">c. 900–965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hieronymus-von-colloredo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hieronymus-von-colloredo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hieronymus von Colloredo</span><span class="tp">1732–1812</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-etienne-cartier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-etienne-cartier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George-Étienne Cartier</span><span class="tp">1814–1873</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
